WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:04.850
All right, my friends, I am so glad you were
with me today, because we are going to need

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:10.750
a full week to unravel and talk through this
election the next weeks, months, years.

00:00:10.750 --> 00:00:16.770
But the big news, of course, coming over the
weekend, multiple networks finally calling

00:00:16.770 --> 00:00:19.430
the presidential election for Joe Biden.

00:00:19.430 --> 00:00:24.590
Joe Biden has defeated Donald Trump and will
be the forty sixth president of the United

00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:29.800
States, defeating Donald Trump by roughly
four point five million votes in the popular

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:30.800
vote.

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:34.050
We're still waiting on final numbers from
some states, but as of now, two hundred and

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:37.090
ninety to 214 in the Electoral College.

00:00:37.090 --> 00:00:42.760
Georgia expected to push that to three hundred
and six electoral votes, the same number that

00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:49.110
Donald Trump had in 2016, which at the time
he and Kellyanne Conway and others described

00:00:49.110 --> 00:00:52.980
as a massive landslide victory.

00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:58.840
And the world, with some few exceptions, has
breathed a collective sigh of relief.

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:04.630
It took days for networks to get comfortable
enough with the margin in Pennsylvania and

00:01:04.630 --> 00:01:06.790
Nevada to call the election.

00:01:06.790 --> 00:01:10.970
But they did on Saturday morning, leading
to the spontaneous breakout of happy people

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:14.520
singing and dancing in the streets quite literally
all over the world.

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:16.409
The communism didn't break out.

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:18.470
The suburbs weren't destroyed.

00:01:18.470 --> 00:01:23.060
Toilets still flushed just once and worked
well enough.

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:28.400
But despite all of the things Trump said would
happen, that didn't happen.

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:32.830
Mostly masks at the events that broke out,
although some real concerns about coronavirus.

00:01:32.830 --> 00:01:34.820
And we're going we're going to get to that.

00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:37.810
Joe Biden will become the 43rd president.

00:01:37.810 --> 00:01:43.159
Senator Kamala Harris, now Vice President
elect Kamala Harris, will become the first

00:01:43.159 --> 00:01:48.670
woman in the White House as president or vice
president in the history of the United States.

00:01:48.670 --> 00:01:55.170
Her husband will become the first ever second
gentleman of the United States, the first

00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:59.810
Jewish person, man or woman as spouse of a
president or VP.

00:01:59.810 --> 00:02:04.640
Now, despite this, Donald Trump has not yet
conceded the election.

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:07.619
Remember, concession is an irrelevant formality.

00:02:07.619 --> 00:02:13.670
It is legally irrelevant, but concession is
what you would expect an adult to do.

00:02:13.670 --> 00:02:18.590
Donald Trump continues to tweet, insists that
this was a stolen election, that there was

00:02:18.590 --> 00:02:23.430
fraud or, as he says, fraud like a petulant
child.

00:02:23.430 --> 00:02:25.890
And there is no telling how much longer he
will keep going.

00:02:25.890 --> 00:02:32.480
He's even being reportedly pressured by Rudy
Giuliani and others to heart to start holding

00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:33.910
rallies again.

00:02:33.910 --> 00:02:39.810
Rallies not about people voting for him, but
rallies to build pressure for I guess recounts

00:02:39.810 --> 00:02:42.620
will have more about that maybe tomorrow.

00:02:42.620 --> 00:02:44.680
But just remember.

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:49.960
Come January 20th, twenty twenty one, Donald
Trump will no longer be president, but for

00:02:49.960 --> 00:02:56.510
now he won't stop truly making a fool out
of himself, tweeting such gems as, quote,

00:02:56.510 --> 00:03:01.760
Since when does the lame stream media call
who our next president will be?

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:05.400
We have all learned a lot in the last two
weeks.

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:11.860
Will remember when they called it for him
with far fewer electoral votes, not even 270

00:03:11.860 --> 00:03:14.500
actually back in 2016.

00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:16.110
He gladly accepted it.

00:03:16.110 --> 00:03:18.450
Trump also tweeting in all caps.

00:03:18.450 --> 00:03:21.720
The observers were not allowed into the counting
rooms.

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:27.180
I won the election got seventy one million
legal votes.

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:34.520
Bad things happened, which our observers were
not allowed to see, never happened before.

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:39.440
Millions of mail in ballots were sent to people
who never asked for them.

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:41.090
Now, that's not true.

00:03:41.090 --> 00:03:44.099
There were Republican and Democratic observers
everywhere.

00:03:44.099 --> 00:03:47.700
This concept of illegal votes is a disgusting
concept.

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:51.490
Something is either a vote from a person or
it is not.

00:03:51.490 --> 00:03:57.269
Trump also tweeting, I won this election by
a lot.

00:03:57.269 --> 00:04:02.390
Why have Trump and Republicans accepted the
results from the House and Senate, but not

00:04:02.390 --> 00:04:04.349
the presidential results?

00:04:04.349 --> 00:04:09.890
Everything was on the same ballots, my friends,
and almost poetic was the news that at the

00:04:09.890 --> 00:04:14.769
time networks called the election Saturday
morning, Donald Trump was golfing.

00:04:14.769 --> 00:04:18.930
Now, as far as Trump's next two months, he
might as well stay on the golf course for

00:04:18.930 --> 00:04:23.659
all I care, to be perfectly frank, multiple
reports are that Trump's inner circle has

00:04:23.659 --> 00:04:27.939
been trying to figure out who's going to go
in and tell him to concede.

00:04:27.939 --> 00:04:32.460
Reportedly, his son in law, Jared Kushner,
trying to get him to concede maybe, although

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:37.169
contrasting reports that Kushner is saying
start doing rallies.

00:04:37.169 --> 00:04:40.210
His wife reportedly, at least for now, his
wife.

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:43.900
We will see what happens with that after the
presidency is over.

00:04:43.900 --> 00:04:49.630
Melania Trump reportedly also saying you should
concede, save some face, but others, like

00:04:49.630 --> 00:04:51.939
Rudy telling him, do rallies.

00:04:51.939 --> 00:04:54.580
So the focus now shifts to the Senate.

00:04:54.580 --> 00:04:56.849
There will be two runoff elections in Georgia.

00:04:56.849 --> 00:05:01.020
Those will ultimately decide who controls
the Senate for Joe Biden's first two years.

00:05:01.020 --> 00:05:02.649
I will talk about that a little later.

00:05:02.649 --> 00:05:08.229
Now, let's understand how good this is, but
also the limits problems aren't solved because

00:05:08.229 --> 00:05:09.470
Trump is leaving.

00:05:09.470 --> 00:05:11.139
We will all be staying vigilant.

00:05:11.139 --> 00:05:14.550
We will all be keeping the Biden Harris administration
accountable.

00:05:14.550 --> 00:05:16.270
And we have to deal with the virus.

00:05:16.270 --> 00:05:19.789
We may not have the Senate, but this is a
major accomplishment.

00:05:19.789 --> 00:05:22.819
It's OK to hold two conflicting feelings.

00:05:22.819 --> 00:05:28.569
This is news worthy of rejoicing about removing
an incumbent president is difficult when we

00:05:28.569 --> 00:05:30.210
talk about the power of incumbency.

00:05:30.210 --> 00:05:31.759
It's not a talking point.

00:05:31.759 --> 00:05:33.270
It's a real thing.

00:05:33.270 --> 00:05:38.439
And yet at the same time, we still have so
many problems that now the work begins and

00:05:38.439 --> 00:05:40.159
it will be big work.

00:05:40.159 --> 00:05:44.069
There will also be plenty of time to talk
about the problems of the Democratic Party

00:05:44.069 --> 00:05:51.550
because to be perfectly clear, massive recession,
record GDP decline, explosive unemployment

00:05:51.550 --> 00:05:57.389
rate out of control, rent foreclosure crisis,
abject failure and dealing with a pandemic.

00:05:57.389 --> 00:05:59.809
And Democrats barely got the presidency.

00:05:59.809 --> 00:06:04.039
It came down to under one hundred thousand
votes in three states.

00:06:04.039 --> 00:06:07.960
You could say it came down to under 50000
votes in two states.

00:06:07.960 --> 00:06:10.020
It's unclear who will control the Senate.

00:06:10.020 --> 00:06:15.080
So the Democratic Party eke this out just
barely and almost blew it.

00:06:15.080 --> 00:06:17.430
And we have to talk about that as well.

00:06:17.430 --> 00:06:19.689
It's not just the Democratic Party.

00:06:19.689 --> 00:06:22.300
Trump ism has not been defeated.

00:06:22.300 --> 00:06:26.520
Trump got more than 70 million votes and we
will talk about that.

00:06:26.520 --> 00:06:32.870
So this should feel like what it is a great
start and this is how progress is made.

00:06:32.870 --> 00:06:38.409
We are all correct to feel a combination of
panic and despair at 70 million people saying

00:06:38.409 --> 00:06:43.300
give me another four years of Trump, but this
is when the work starts and we'll be going

00:06:43.300 --> 00:07:43.300
through 

00:07:43.300 --> 00:07:52.689
all of it.

